How the automatic narrator works (and its limits)
Before speaking, the player divides stories into performance beats, identifies quoted dialogue and likely speakers, and estimates semantic intention, energy, tension, warmth, and narrative distance. It chooses a performance mode and speech rate, pitch, volume, voice (when multiple device voices are available), and pause length per beat. In radio-style dialogue, it omits some written speech attributions so characters speak directly. It gradually moves from adventure to quiet bedtime narration.
This is a local, rule-based semantic scoring prototype—not a connected AI model. It interprets cues automatically but may occasionally mistake a character or emotional tone. Distinct character voices depend on available iPhone/browser speech voices and may fall back to a single voice with pitch and pacing changes. This is not a cinematic audio mixer. The reading uses your device's built-in speech synthesis, so audio stays on the device and no audio file is created. Safari may require the page to be opened as a website, rather than in a file preview.
For ChatGPT Voice, the assistant can write and direct scenes adaptively in this chat, but cannot directly switch the app’s underlying voice or guarantee actor-like synthesis. This standalone theater has its own device-dependent speech behavior.
